00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:57.209
Derek Meyer: Subgraphs would… are a flagship product.

59
00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:17.140
Derek Meyer: Those were made to be reorg-aware from day one, and it will constantly look at what the latest block is, compare block hashes, identify when a reorg has occurred. It has proper versioning of entities to be able to roll back a few, a few blocks, and then replay those blocks correctly, and that way your database is,

60
00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:20.969
Derek Meyer: You know, is totally fine, or only contains canonical information.

61
00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:31.130
Derek Meyer: More recently, from the auditability perspective, we've had the request of, if there was inaccurate information that got to your database.

62
00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:37.170
Derek Meyer: We wanted to implement some custom handling, and that way, we don't actually delete that data from the database.

63
00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:54.249
Derek Meyer: But instead, we invalidate it in the database and maintain that, so as to achieve full auditability, in case a user says, I was accessing the website in it, or the application in it showed me that my balance was X. We can fully go through and say, yep, at time X,

64
00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:59.739
