83
00:12:28.020 --> 00:12:39.690
Derek Meyer: This all gets written into a, an object storage, in different flat files, and then you have your transform layer, right? Transform layer would be your substreams.

84
00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:54.169
Derek Meyer: This allows you to go and access those flat files in parallel. You can horizontally scale up however many worker nodes you want, so if you aren't in a rush, you could have one worker, and it's just kind of going linearly, which is how subgraphs do now.

